{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Yehudah went down from his brothers.</b> He went away, for he could not bear his father's grief. Here Rashi explained: they brought him down from his greatness. And that is what is written — <b>מאת אחיו</b>, that is to say, through his brothers. And if you ask: is there not from this descent until our fathers went down to Egypt twenty-two years, and how could it happen that within that time Yehudah's wife bore Er and Onan and Shelah, and it is written 'and the days multiplied and the daughter of Shua died,' etc., and afterward Tamar conceived and bore Peretz and Zerach, and Peretz fathered Chetzron and Chamul before they went down to Egypt? The answer to the matter: there is nothing to wonder at, for the early generations would father children at seven years, and these did likewise, as is stated in Seder Olam: how so? One year went for the conception of Er, another for Onan, another for Shelah. Er grew up and waited seven years and married Tamar — that is eight years from when Yehudah went down until 'and Er was evil and He put him to death.' The ninth year Onan married, and in that same year he died. The tenth year went for the growing of Shelah, as it is stated: 'remain a widow in your father's house,' etc. The eleventh year — 'and the days multiplied,' when Shelah grew up and he did not marry her, and he told Tamar, etc., until 'and he came to her and she conceived by him.' The twelfth year went for the conception of Peretz and Zerach; and Peretz waited seven years and married a wife — that is nineteen years from when Yehudah went down. The twentieth year went for the conception of Chetzron, and the twenty-first for that of Chamul, and in the twenty-second year Chamul was born, and he and Chetzron his brother went down with their fathers to Egypt."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:51.742740840Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}